---
# Serial Studio clang-tidy configuration.
#
# Makes the repo's own style contract the authority for every clang-tidy run: Qt Creator's bundled
# clang-tidy/clangd, an LLVM install, and scripts/clang-tidy-verify.py all read this file, so a check
# that fights doc/claude/code-style.md (enforced by scripts/code-verify.py and .clang-format) is off
# here once instead of being re-silenced per IDE. Findings are advisories, never a gate.
#
# Opt-in by family (-* first); the vendor families (altera, boost, fuchsia, llvm, llvmlibc, abseil,
# android, zircon, mpi, openmp, objc, darwin, linuxkernel, hicpp) are off by omission. hicpp is
# mostly aliases plus hicpp-signed-bitwise, which fires on every Qt::CTRL | Qt::Key_X.
#
# Disabled inside the enabled families, one reason each:
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters    (int, int) geometry and index signatures everywhere
#   cert-err58-cpp                          static QString / QStringLiteral objects are the idiom
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays        alias of modernize-avoid-c-arrays (kept), one report
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members
#                                           spec-0070 sub-objects bind their facade by reference
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while        the SS_ASSERT family is do/while(0) by contract
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers   alias of readability-magic-numbers (off, below)
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
#                                           code-verify --singleton-census ratchets global state
#   cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage           the assertion and optimizer macros are the design
#   cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions alias of bugprone-narrowing-conversions (kept)
#   cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#                                           alias of the misc- check (off, below)
#   cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory         Qt parent ownership, not gsl::owner
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay
#                                           every tr("...") and const char* API decays a literal
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index
#                                           wants gsl::at
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic
#                                           byte-level frame parsing is pointer arithmetic
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast
#                                           invariant-checked static_cast replaces dynamic_cast on
#                                           the hotpath (code-style.md, Power of Ten rule 9)
#   cppcoreguidelines-use-default-member-init
#                                           alias of the modernize- check (off, below)
#   cppcoreguidelines-use-enum-class        Q_ENUM enums exposed to QML stay unscoped
#   misc-include-cleaner                    OFF ON PURPOSE: Qt umbrella headers (<QtCore>,
#                                           <QCoreApplication>) and the lib/ forwarding headers make
#                                           nearly every Qt symbol "not directly included", so the
#                                           signal is all noise here; re-enable per file if needed
#   misc-no-recursion                       recursion is allowed with a hard depth cap (rule 1)
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#                                           push descriptors and payload structs are plain data
#   misc-use-anonymous-namespace            file-local helpers are `static` free functions here
#   modernize-raw-string-literal            lupdate-visible strings stay escaped literals
#   modernize-use-default-member-init       code-style.md forbids in-header member init
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers   positional aggregate init of push/candidate structs
#   modernize-use-ranges                    not adopted
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type      not the repo shape
#   performance-enum-size                   moc / QML enums must stay int-sized
#   portability-simd-intrinsics             core/Core/DSPSimd.h is the one intrinsics home
#   readability-avoid-const-params-in-decls header declarations mirror their definitions
#   readability-braces-around-statements    RemoveBracesLLVM strips single-statement braces
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity, readability-function-size
#                                           code-verify.py owns the function and TU caps
#   readability-identifier-length           r, a, b, lo, hi, it, n are the geometry idiom
#   readability-magic-numbers               named where a name exists; kCamelCase is enforced by
#                                           the naming check instead of by a literal hunt
#   readability-redundant-access-specifiers header order repeats `private:` (helpers, members)
#   readability-uppercase-literal-suffix    lowercase suffixes are the repo shape
#
# Option notes: readability-implicit-bool-conversion allows pointer conditions (`if (ptr)` is the
# Qt idiom); readability-simplify-boolean-expr leaves `!a || !b` guard chains alone (folding them
# hides which guard fired); special-member-functions accepts a sole default dtor and a deleted copy
# without moves (Q_DISABLE_COPY shape).
#
# Naming (doc/claude/code-style.md table, plus what the tree actually does): types, enums and
# namespaces CamelCase (`detail` is the one accepted lowercase sub-namespace, 14 first-party files);
# methods camelBack; free functions camelBack or lower_case (the DataModel kernels: uniform_grid,
# clone_block_trimmed); params and locals lower_case or camelBack (both shapes ship: frame_data and
# sourceId); private members m_camelBack; public/protected members lower_case or camelBack;
# file-scope statics s_lower_case; function-local statics also accept the camelBack
# `static auto& x = X::instance()` cache (1000+ sites); constants kCamelCase, with UPPER_CASE
# accepted the way code-verify's file-scope constant rule accepts it; macros UPPER_CASE.
#
# Header filter: first-party roots only (core/, app/src, app/tests); lib/, the ThirdParty trees and
# build dirs are excluded. A nested .clang-tidy in a vendored tree may set `Checks: '-*'` on its own;
# one that sets `InheritParentConfig: true` layers its keys on top of this file instead.

Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  cert-*,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-use-default-member-init,
  -cppcoreguidelines-use-enum-class,
  google-build-namespaces,
  google-build-using-namespace,
  google-default-arguments,
  google-explicit-constructor,
  google-global-names-in-headers,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-raw-string-literal,
  -modernize-use-default-member-init,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -modernize-use-ranges,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  -portability-simd-intrinsics,
  readability-*,
  -readability-avoid-const-params-in-decls,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-function-size,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-redundant-access-specifiers,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '[/\\](core|app[/\\]src|app[/\\]tests)[/\\]'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '([/\\]lib[/\\]|[/\\]ThirdParty[/\\]|[/\\]build[/\\]|_deps)'
FormatStyle: file
SystemHeaders: false

CheckOptions:
  cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions.AllowSoleDefaultDtor: true
  cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions.AllowMissingMoveFunctionsWhenCopyIsDeleted: true
  readability-implicit-bool-conversion.AllowPointerConditions: true
  readability-implicit-bool-conversion.AllowIntegerConditions: false
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr.SimplifyDeMorgan: false
  modernize-use-nodiscard.ReplacementString: '[[nodiscard]]'
  readability-identifier-naming.IgnoreMainLikeFunctions: true
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceIgnoredRegexp: '^detail$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.UnionCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TemplateParameterCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalFunctionCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalFunctionIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(_[a-z0-9]+)+$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$'
  readability-identifier-naming.LocalVariableCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.LocalVariableIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$'
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticVariableCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticVariableIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$'
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalVariableCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalVariablePrefix: s_
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassMemberPrefix: s_
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix: m_
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$'
  readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariablePrefix: k
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableIgnoredRegexp: '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$'
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantPrefix: k
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantIgnoredRegexp: '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$'
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantPrefix: k
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantIgnoredRegexp: '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantPrefix: k
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantIgnoredRegexp: '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$'
  readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionIgnoredRegexp: '^[A-Z]+(_[A-Z]+)*_$'
